  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Securing the conservation of globally-significant wild cat landscapes in northern, north-eastern and western India through a landscape conservation approach for wild cats that brings together species conservation programs, connects stakeholders and empowers communities, and operates across PAs, tiger corridors and buffer zones. Along with integrating small cat needs into existing large cat conservation initiatives so that all wild cats are considered together.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) gaps in the policy, planning and procedural framework, 2) limited capacity at State, landscape and site levels, 3) lack of understanding and incentives to support community engagement in wild cat conservation, and 4) insufficient partnerships, regional coordination and outreach to engage the corporate sector, strengthen transboundary collaboration and support knowledge exchange.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	Project Inception Workshops conducted at national and sub-national levels to engage all relevant stakeholders and get their recommendations towards project implementation. 
2.	Process initiated for the development of &#x2018;Landscape conservation master plans for wild cats&#x2019;, for Dudhwa and Pakke-Eaglenest landscapes.
3.	Process initiated for the development of &#x2018;Species Recovery Plans&#x2019;, for Caracal, Fishing Cat and Clouded Leopard.
4.	Discussions conducted and process initiated for the development of a national-level database/Atlas for small wild cats in India.
5.	Regional &amp; National level meetings conducted, and process initiated towards the establishment of a &#x2018;National green business platform&#x2019;, aimed at engaging the corporate sector in conservation initiatives benefiting wild cats and their habitats.
6.	At least 6 conservation-based best practices documented from the project landscapes, intended for dissemination and upscaling.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Key Results for the year 2022 include the following:
1. Project Inception Workshops successfully conducted at National and sub-national level on 16 November and 20 December respectively, with the involvement and active participation of all the key project stakeholders. Inception Report shared and uploaded on PIMS.
2. Landscape level strategy document for small wild cat conservation in India developed. The strategy document clearly defines the process and approach for the development of &#x2018;Landscape conservation master plans for wild cats&#x2019; and its institutionalization in India.
3. Concept developed for the national level database for small wild cats along with mobile application for promoting citizen science in India. The national database and application shall now be operationalized and is expected to become the national tool to monitor small wild cat populations in India
4. Strategy paper developed for private sector engagement in wildlife conservation prepared as part of the National-level Green Business Platform.
5. First Regional Consultation for the National-level Green Business Platform scheduled on 28 December 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Local Project Appraisal Committee (LPAC) is yet to be convened for the project. The AWP and the targets will be uploaded post the same.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Local Project Appraisal Committee (LPAC) meeting was convened on 6 December 2021 for the project. The AWP will be uploaded after the prodoc is signed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
